however, it is also possible for these drugs to influence cognitive processes beyond just mood regulation, leading to increased risk-taking behaviors or impulsivity. For example, antidepressants like sertraline (paroxetine) have been shown to increase aggression and violence among those who take them regularly over time.

ultimately, while medication alone cannot guarantee suicide prevention, its use should be carefully monitored with close attention paid to potential adverse effects on mental health and overall well-being. It's always best to consult with healthcare professionals before starting any new treatment plan.


