What is the difference between HTML and JavaScript?

[Response A]
HTML (Hypertext Markup Language) defines the structure of an electronic document, including its title, headings, paragraphs, lists, images, videos, audio files, etc.

JavaScript (Java Script), on the other hand, is a programming language that allows developers to manipulate web pages by executing code in response to user input or events such as mouse clicks, keyboard strokes, touch events, etc. It can also interact with external resources like databases, APIs, and network protocols. 

In summary, while both HTML and JavaScript work together to create dynamic websites, they serve different purposes: HTML provides structural information about how your website should look and functionally; whereas JavaScript enables interactive elements within those structures.

[Response B]
